WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.700
You've set who you may contact, and
only a person can grant consent.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.467
Now you decide who comes first. Score
ranks every account on fit and intent,

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.667
and shows the evidence
behind each verdict.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.767
You know who to call before they call.

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:14.800
In this clip you'll read a verdict,
change the model behind it,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.033
and watch it learn from outcomes.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:20.200
Score is an engine: logic that
runs on your signed definitions,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.633
never on hidden rules.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.500
Mia's team has more accounts than hours.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.433
Without Score, the list
is whoever shouted last,

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:28.900
and last quarter's funding
round still looks like news.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.367
Score fixes that with
reasons you can read.

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:32.633
First, the composite.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:35.833
Fit is how closely a company
matches your ideal customer profile.

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:39.000
Intent is what it did lately:
a funding round, a hiring push,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:39.900
a pricing page visit.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.467
Score weighs both into one composite
and maps it to Hot, Warm or Cold.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:46.533
Every weight and threshold
lives in a signed definition,

00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.367
so you can read the rule behind a rank.

00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:51.367
Second, intent fades, so
old news stops counting.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.867
Every signal loses weight on
a half life set by its family.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.833
By default web intent fades in about two

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:57.767
weeks and a funding round in about six.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:02.067
Signals seen first hand count more. A
retracted signal counts for nothing,

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.233
and in Strict mode so
does an unverified one.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.767
Third, the brakes. A hard
disqualifier caps a score,

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.233
such as a former customer or a
competitor on your suppression list.

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:13.467
The lowest cap wins, and a cap
of zero zeroes the account.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:17.133
Negatives lower intent: an unsubscribe,
an objection, a hard bounce.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.500
Missing data is never punished.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.933
An unknown field is left out of
the score, not counted as zero.

00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:23.733
Fourth, the committee and the clock.

00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:27.467
Coverage counts how many roles on
the largest open deal you've engaged,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:31.133
and flags a missing champion. That's
why buying roles mattered last clip.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.700
And a band decays when
nobody touches the account.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.033
By default Hot slides to
Warm after three days,

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.900
and Warm to Cold after fourteen.

00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:41.367
Now read a verdict. In the console:
CRM, Hot list, click an account.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.233
The why drawer lists what lifted
it and what pulled it down.

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:47.933
It shows the caps, the negatives,
how far each signal has decayed,

00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:49.333
and who on the committee is covered.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.733
Or ask your agent: "Show the hot
list and why number one is hot".

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.333
To score on demand, open Engines, Score.

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:59.167
You'll see Accounts to score,
Qualifications, Rescan, KPIs and Learning,

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:03.000
and a Lead queue ranked by band,
segment and committee coverage.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.667
Or ask your agent: "Score Northwind
Logistics and explain it".

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.867
Now change the model.

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:10.367
One definition kind, the
scoring model, with three keys:

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.500
default for qualification,
ICP fit for firmographic fit,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.833
and signals for signal strength.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.800
Mia says what good looks like,
Orbit drafts it, Sophia signs it.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.067
Your definitions, signed once.

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:22.900
In the console, review the plan on the
Environments page. Or ask your agent:

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.200
"Propose raising the weight of
funding signals in our scoring model".

00:02:26.233 --> 00:02:27.933
Power habit: preview before you commit.

00:02:27.933 --> 00:02:30.967
A new signed version rescans
the whole organization.

00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:33.400
The rescan preview scores
accounts and rolls every one back,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.600
so nothing is written
and nothing is queued.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.867
It shows who moves into or out
of qualified, the band changes,

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:41.967
and which handoffs would fire. Ask
your agent: "Preview the rescore".

00:02:41.967 --> 00:02:44.400
Run it before a model change
and before an upgrade.

00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:46.833
Score also learns, with
a person in the loop.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.633
Weekly, Learning measures
lift per criterion:

00:02:48.633 --> 00:02:51.767
how much more often accounts
with it replied, booked or won.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.633
It needs verdicts at least thirty

00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:56.100
days old and ninety
five percent confidence.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.767
A weight moves at most thirty percent
a run, and disqualifiers never change.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.700
The result is a proposed version
that a different person approves.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.900
In the console: Engines, Score, Learning.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.867
Or ask your agent: "Propose a
scoring update from outcomes".

00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:09.000
Reps teach it too.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.567
In the Lead queue, use Flag this
score when a verdict looks wrong.

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:15.467
Rep flags are learning inputs,
and agent flags are not.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.500
Shadow accuracy keeps Score
honest. In Settings, Safety,

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.133
the CRM write back card compares past

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.233
qualified verdicts with
the deals that followed.

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:24.900
It says so when the sample is too small.

00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:27.433
The dashboard shows accounts
scored, the tier mix,

00:03:27.433 --> 00:03:29.867
how often reps accept Score's next move,

00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:31.433
and the lift from qualified to deal.

00:03:31.433 --> 00:03:35.033
Rising acceptance with steady lift
means the model fits your market.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.000
When lift fades, open Learning.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.367
Or ask: "How is scoring
performing this month? "

00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:42.433
Score doesn't work alone. Signals
and enriched fields feed it,

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:44.700
and replies and bounces
count as negatives.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.533
A qualified account hands off to Routing
for an owner, to Outreach to enrol,

00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:48.967
and to plays.

00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:52.433
With a CRM of record, scores can
be written back as a proposal.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.900
The honest edge. Learning needs history,

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.367
and with too little it says
insufficient data instead of guessing.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.467
Agent flags don't teach it.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.367
Account based marketing and the wider

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.700
sales intelligence engines
are on the roadmap,

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.833
not in the product.

00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:08.233
The worry: a model that learns
will drift somewhere I can't see.

00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:09.500
It can't change by itself.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.833
A weight cap and a confidence bar
sit between the data and the model.

00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:16.000
Every change arrives as a proposal
that a different person approves.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:18.467
Run it back: Fit and
intent make the composite,

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:21.767
caps and decay keep it honest,
and outcomes tune the weights.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:25.233
Every verdict shows its reasons,
and only a person changes the model.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:28.167
You can now rank accounts, read
the reason for every verdict,

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.733
and let outcomes tune the model. Open
the Hot list and click number one.

00:04:31.733 --> 00:04:34.600
Coming next: Enrichment, which
fills the gaps in your data.
